#: templates/mail-guide.html:61
msgid "Greylisting"
msgstr "Greylisting"

#. Status: source
#. Phase: 1
#: templates/mail-guide.html:62
msgid ""
"Greylisting is off by default, so incoming mail is accepted on the first "
"connection. An administrator can turn it on to cut down on spam. When "
"greylisting is on, your box initially rejects mail from people you "
"haven&rsquo;t received mail from before. Legitimate mail servers attempt "
"redelivery shortly afterwards, but most spam does not. Mail from someone "
"new, such as a confirmation while you are registering on a website, can "
"then be delayed by at least 3 minutes, depending on when the remote "
"server retries."
msgstr ""
"Greylisting is off by default, so incoming mail is accepted on the first "
"connection. An administrator can turn it on to cut down on spam. When "
"greylisting is on, your box initially rejects mail from people you "
"haven&rsquo;t received mail from before. Legitimate mail servers attempt "
"redelivery shortly afterwards, but most spam does not. Mail from someone "
"new, such as a confirmation while you are registering on a website, can "
"then be delayed by at least 3 minutes, depending on when the remote "
"server retries."

#. Status: source
#. Phase: 1
#: templates/mail-guide.html:64
msgid "Loading greylisting setting..."
msgstr "Loading greylisting setting..."

#. Status: source
#. Phase: 1
#: templates/mail-guide.html:94
msgid "+tag addresses"
msgstr "+tag addresses"

#. Status: source
#. Phase: 1
#: templates/mail-guide.html:95
msgid ""
"Every incoming email address also receives mail for <code>+tag</code> "
"addresses. If your email address is <code>you@yourdomain.com</code>, "
"you&rsquo;ll also automatically get mail sent to "
"<code>you+anythinghere@yourdomain.com</code>. Use this as a fast way to "
"segment incoming mail for your own filtering rules without having to "
"create aliases in this control panel."
msgstr ""
"Every incoming email address also receives mail for <code>+tag</code> "
"addresses. If your email address is <code>you@yourdomain.com</code>, "
"you&rsquo;ll also automatically get mail sent to "
"<code>you+anythinghere@yourdomain.com</code>. Use this as a fast way to "
"segment incoming mail for your own filtering rules without having to "
"create aliases in this control panel."

#. Status: source
#. Phase: 1
#: templates/mail-guide.html:97
msgid "Use only this box to send as you"
msgstr "Use only this box to send as you"

#. Status: source
#. Phase: 1
#: templates/mail-guide.html:98
msgid ""
"Your box sets strict email sending policies for your domain names to make"
" it harder for spam and other fraudulent mail to claim to be you. Only "
"this machine is authorized to send email on behalf of your domain names. "
"If you use any other service to send email as you, it will likely get "
"spam filtered by recipients."
msgstr ""
"Your box sets strict email sending policies for your domain names to make"
" it harder for spam and other fraudulent mail to claim to be you. Only "
"this machine is authorized to send email on behalf of your domain names. "
"If you use any other service to send email as you, it will likely get "
"spam filtered by recipients."

